1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:03,800
READING AND SPEAKING TASK

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:07,680
THE MILLION-Pound BANK NOTE

3
00:00:07,680 --> 00:00:10,900
ACT II, SCENE IV

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:15,940
At the end of the month, Henry was very rich and didn't fear jail.

5
00:00:16,740 --> 00:00:17,940
Dressed in the finest clothes,

6
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:20,560
he drove by the brother's house in Portland Place,

7
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:21,300
and,

8
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:24,840
seeing they were back, went to get Portia at her friend's home.

9
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,480
My dear, the way you look today,

10
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:33,300
it would be a crime not to ask for a good salary for the job they'll give to me.

11
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,520
Oh, please remember that if we ask for too much,

12
00:00:37,540 --> 00:00:41,260
we may get no salary at all, and then what'll happen to us

13
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:43,460
with no way in the world to earn a living?

14
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,900
Good morning, gentlemen. Portia,

15
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,660
these are the men who helped me.

16
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:51,700
So very nice to meet you, kind sirs.

17
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,960
Gentlemen, I'm ready to report.

18
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,080
Err, Portia, I...

19
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:00,860
We're both glad to hear it. For now we can decide the bet

20
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:02,460
which Roderick and I made.

21
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:06,540
If you've won for me, you shall have any job as my gift.

22
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:09,080
Have you got the million-pound bank note?

23
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:10,960
Here it is, sir.

24
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:14,540
I've won! Now what do you say, Roderick?

25
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:20,160
I say that I've lost twenty thousand pounds. I never would have believed it.

26
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:22,960
Why, that is amazing, man.

27
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,040
Come, let's be going now, Portia.

28
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:30,960
But wait, wait, the job, you know. I must give you a job,

29
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,140
as I promised.

30
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:36,380
Well, thank you very much, but I really don't want one now.

31
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:40,040
Henry, I'm disappointed in you.

32
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:42,240
You didn't thank the gentleman properly.

33
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:43,200
May I do it

34
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:43,780
for you?

35
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:45,520
Let me see you try.

36
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,400
Portia walks over to Roderick and gives him a hug.

37
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,540
Then she sits in Oliver's lap,

38
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,680
puts her arms around his neck and kisses him on the cheek.

39
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,640
Oliver begins laughing.

40
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:02,400
Papa, he says he doesn't want anything else from you.

41
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:05,500
My dear, is that your papa?

42
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:09,220
He's my stepfather and the dearest one that ever was.

43
00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:15,040
Oh, my dearest, dear sir, I regret what I said. You have got a job open

44
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:15,820
that I want.

45
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:17,060
Name it.

46
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:18,260
Son-in-law.

47
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:22,840
Well, well, well. But you've never had such a job before.

48
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:26,100
How can I be sure you can do it successfully?

49
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:31,280
Try me. Oh, do, I beg of you. Give me thirty or forty years and-

50
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:32,960
Oh, well, all right.

51
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:35,160
Are Portia and Henry happy?

52
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:39,160
There are not enough words in the biggest dictionary to describe it.

53
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,920
Did the people of London have a good time with this bit of news?

54
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:48,120
Yes. Portia's stepfather took that banknote back to the Bank of England

55
00:02:48,120 --> 00:02:49,080
and cashed it.

56
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,200
The banknote was then useless for money,

57
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:54,500
but was his wedding gift to the young couple.

58
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:58,040
Yes, the banknote was worth millions of dollars,

59
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:02,360
but not worth one-tenth as much as how Henry felt about Portia.
